en:
You stopped in your tracks.{w}No -- you could not go one step further.{w}{p}The monster that had been about to cross your path
noticed its prey and clattered its jawbone.{w}It was a symbol of death, notorious even among adventurers.{w}{p}Why had it appeared here?{w}Why, gripped by such terror, could you not move?{w}Why did it have to be you who ran into it?{w}{p}All manner of thoughts must have flashed through your minds.{w}But there is no need to worry.{w}{p}However much you rage at the injustice of it,{w}however much you tremble in fear,{w}it will all be over in a matter of moments.{w}{p}Had it been waiting for you to steel yourselves?{w}Bones rattling in the silence, the dreadful monster
slowly raised its scythe...{w}

{0E}"I just have to kill them, right?
Kill these guys and you'll be satisfied, right...{0F}
Numbra Narv!!"{w}

{0E}You held up the Light Rank you had obtained
in the Sanctum of Genesis.{0F}
Rafa's body was enveloped in a warm light.{w}{p}The Sun Spirit who guards the True Crystal
began to shine brighter than ever before.{w}

"Ah, what wonderful power...{w}Now I won't have to burn up my own life...{w}I can keep on shining forever...!"{w}{p}"It wasn't the suffering itself I hated."{w}{p}"What hurt was not being able to keep shining
on all the people of this land I love so dearly."{w}{p}"...But thanks to all of you,
it looks like I can shine on them forever now."{w}

Hand in hand, Rafa and Yorfa would surely
go on protecting this land.{w}{p}Along with the warm light, a deep, gentle sense
of fulfillment wrapped around you.{w}

"The Palace of the Sun draws ever closer
to our world, the Dark Realm.
All according to Master Mayer's will..."{w}

"Such things are of no consequence."{w}{p}"Serving not a god but Master Mayer,
and touching the deaths of mortals...
that, for me, is the greatest of joys..."{w}
